            {
              "text": "For an executor handling a deceased estate in Brisbane’s Southside, engaging a law firm located within or close to **Mount Gravatt** and **Sunnybank** provides convenient access for certifying documents, reviewing original wills, and managing property or bank transfers.\n\nSeveral well-established firms in the immediate Mount Gravatt and Sunnybank areas specialize in Queensland succession law, Supreme Court probate, and deceased estate administration:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Law Firms in Sunnybank & Sunnybank Hills\n\n* **Wheldon & Associates (Sunnybank)**\n  * **Location:** Zamia Street, Sunnybank\n  * **Expertise:** Deeply experienced in deceased estate administration. They routinely assist executors with Supreme Court applications for Grants of Probate and Letters of Administration, notifying institutions (Centrelink, banks, share registries), transferring/selling estate real estate, and distributing inheritances.\n* **Denovo Lawyers (Sunnybank / Sunnybank Hills)**\n  * **Location:** Sunnybank Hills\n  * **Expertise:** Handles estate administration, probate applications, and transmission of property. They also offer multilingual assistance (including Mandarin/Cantonese), which is helpful if any beneficiaries or paperwork involve overseas or cross-border assets.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Law Firms in Mount Gravatt & Upper Mount Gravatt\n\n* **Campbells Legal Services (Upper Mount Gravatt)**\n  * **Location:** Upper Mount Gravatt\n  * **Expertise:** Focuses heavily on wills and deceased estates. They guide executors step-by-step through probate requirements, executor duties, compliance with Queensland succession statutes, and distribution.\n* **Anthonys Lawyers (Upper Mount Gravatt)**\n  * **Location:** 1681 Logan Road, Upper Mount Gravatt\n  * **Expertise:** Established in the area since 1977. They maintain an active estate administration practice, assisting executors with formal grants of probate, letters of administration, title transfers, and closing out accounts.\n* **Elliott & Harvey Lawyers (Upper Mount Gravatt)**\n  * **Location:** 1953 Logan Road, Upper Mount Gravatt\n  * **Expertise:** A longstanding Southside boutique firm operating since 1975 with dedicated deceased estates and succession law services for executors.\n* **Bennett Carroll Solicitors (Upper Mount Gravatt)**\n  * **Location:** Upper Mount Gravatt\n  * **Expertise:** A full-service firm with a major southside hub handling estate litigation, probate filings in the Supreme Court, and estate asset realization.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Dedicated Queensland Estate Specialists (Brisbane-Wide)\n\nIf the estate has complicated family trusts, business interests, or potential family provision disputes, you may also consider dedicated estate boutique firms:\n* **de Groots Wills and Estate Lawyers:** One of Queensland’s oldest specialist wills and estate firms.\n* **The Estate Lawyers:** A Queensland practice exclusively dedicated to estate administration, probate, and estate litigation.\n\n---\n\n### Practical Considerations for Executors in Queensland\n\n1. **Costs are an Estate Expense:** Reasonable legal fees incurred for applying for probate and administering the estate are generally paid out of the estate’s funds, not from your personal pocket.\n2. **Fixed-Fee Probate:** Many Brisbane firms offer a **fixed-fee quote** solely for preparing the probate application, advertising notices (such as the *Queensland Law Reporter* and Supreme Court notices), and obtaining the Grant of Probate.\n3. **Scope of Representation:** Clarify whether you want the solicitor only to obtain the **Grant of Probate** (leaving you to collect and distribute the assets) or to handle the **full estate administration** (closing bank accounts, selling shares, paying estate debts, and distributing funds into trust).",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
